-- title:
--   Vélu quotient of the Tate curve by its toric p-slots
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, $p$ a nonzero natural number which is odd, and $\zeta$ a unit of $K$ whose underlying element is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Assume further that the pair of two-variable series $(\mathtt{tateUnivX},\mathtt{tateUnivY})$ over $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\,\mathbb Z$ — whose coefficients are the explicit divisor-sum and binomial expressions recorded in their definitions — satisfies the affine Weierstrass equation of `tateUnivCurve` $=\langle 1,0,0,\mathtt{tateUnivA4},\mathtt{tateUnivA6}\rangle$, the diagonal lift of the Tate coefficients $\mathtt{tateA4},\mathtt{tateA6}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a Weierstrass variable change $C=(u,r,s,t)$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ with $u$ the constant $p$, $r$ the constant $(p^2-1)/12$, $s$ the constant $(p-1)/2$ and $t$ the constant $-(p^2-1)/24$, such that $C$ carries the Vélu quotient model of `tateBase K p` by the finite set `toricSlotSet K p ζ` exactly onto the image of the Tate curve under $q\mapsto q^{p^2}$. Here `tateBase K p` is the Tate curve $\langle 1,0,0,\mathtt{tateA4},\mathtt{tateA6}\rangle$ with $q$ replaced by $q^p$; the Vélu quotient keeps $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and replaces $a_4$ by $a_4-5\sum_S \mathtt{veluT}$ and $a_6$ by $a_6-b_2\sum_S \mathtt{veluT}-7\sum_S \mathtt{veluW}$; and the slot set is the image of $\{1,\dots,\lfloor p/2\rfloor\}$ under $k\mapsto \mathtt{toricPoint}\,K\,p\,(\zeta^k)$, the explicit pairs of Laurent series with constant terms $c/(1-c)^2$ and $c^2/(1-c)^3$ and higher coefficients the displayed divisor sums over multiples of $p$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion form of the statement that dividing the Tate curve of parameter $q^p$ by its toric subgroup generated by the points with parameters $\zeta^k$ yields, after the indicated rescaling, the Tate curve of parameter $q^{p^2}$; the constants $(p^2-1)/12$ and $-(p^2-1)/24$ absorb the constant terms produced by the Vélu sums, and $u=p$ requires $p$ invertible. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_variableChange_veluQuotient_toricPoint_tateLaurent_map_qExpand_eq_map_qExpand_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_variableChange_veluQuotient_toricPoint_tateLaurent_map_qExpand_eq_map_qExpand_mul) in the construction of the degeneracy/Hecke relations on $q$-expansions underlying the modular curve $X_0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_variableChange_veluQuotient_toricSlotSet.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_TateSlots
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_Velu
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.VariableChange
import Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.PrimitiveRoots

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.exists_variableChange_veluQuotient_toricSlotSet (K : Type*) [Field K]
    [CharZero K] (p : ℕ) [NeZero p] (hp : Odd p) (ζ : Kˣ) (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot (ζ : K) p)
    (hE : tateUnivCurve.toAffine.Equation tateUnivX tateUnivY) :
    ∃ C : WeierstrassCurve.VariableChange (LaurentSeries K),
      (C.u : LaurentSeries K) = (p : LaurentSeries K) ∧
        C.r = HahnSeries.C (((p : K) ^ 2 - 1) / 12) ∧
          C.s = HahnSeries.C (((p : K) - 1) / 2) ∧
            C.t = HahnSeries.C (-(((p : K) ^ 2 - 1) / 24)) ∧
              C • (tateBase K p).veluQuotient (toricSlotSet K p ζ) =
                (tateLaurent K).map (qExpand K (p * p)) := by sorry
